-- Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two, three power armors (printed 83-94): Demon Slayer, Enforcer Guardsman, Firefighter
-- 3 vehicle rows, with 44 locations and 12 weapon entries.
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration - it adds
-- rows, not schema.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/~303-northern-gun-2-power-armor-c.sql
--
-- Written by scripts/vessel-sql.mjs from 1 worker file(s). Every value
-- is printable ASCII, every row cites its book, and a Main Body location
-- agrees with its vehicle's mdc_main_body.

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO vehicles (slug, name, system, vehicle_class, crew, passengers, speed_ground, speed_air, speed_water, dimensions, weight_tons, mdc_main_body, is_mega_damage, ar, cost, cost_note, description, source_book) VALUES
  ('ng-x44-demon-slayer', 'Demon Slayer Power Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One.', NULL, 'Running: 90 mph (144 km) maximum, 20% of the normal fatigue rate at full speed, 10% at 50 mph (80 km) or less. Leaping: 20 ft (6.1 m) high or across unassisted; jet-boosted up to 100 ft (30.5 m) high and 200 ft (61 m) across; +30% with a running start for either. Not flight.', 'None; it cannot hover.', 'Not built for water; walks the bottom at 10 mph (16 km/8.6 knots). Maximum depth 1,000 ft (305 m).', 'Man-sized, to the buyer''s size: height 6-8 ft (1.8 to 2.4 m); width 4.5 ft (1.4 m); length 3.6-4 ft (printed as 2 to 1.2 m)', '682 lbs (307 kg) fully loaded', 200, 1, NULL, 760000, '1 million credits nuclear or 760,000 Solid Oxide; there is no electric battery version. The lowest is stored. Northern Gun works to keep the price low. A replacement silver-coated impaler spike typically runs 1D4x1000 credits. The priced Techno-Wizard conversions are aftermarket work NG never sells (gear rows ng-x44-demon-slayer-tw-lightning-bolt-discharger, -tw-fire-ball-discharger, -tw-light-fire-bolt-gatling, -tw-heavy-fire-bolt-gatling, -tw-wood-shard-gatling, -tw-ice-shard-discharger and -tw-ice-shard-gatling).', 'Model Type: NG-X44. Class: Anti-Demon, Anti-Monster Fighter and Assault Power Armor. Built for one job, hunting demons and other supernatural monsters, rather than NG''s usual all-round versatility, so ordinary infantry power armor, combat robots and vehicles can outgun it. Nearly everything on it is silver-coated or fires wood or silver, and NG keeps it stocked and cheap; Reid''s Rangers, Cyber-Knights and vampire hunters prize it. A row of silver blade-fins runs up the spine to a bladed helmet crest, so anything that jumps on its back takes 5D6 M.D.; the fins and the double sword also make the wearer a hazard to furniture, bystanders and teammates. Its signature is a heavy armored collar on the back carrying two robot gatling arms, copied in spirit from the Coalition Juicer Killer, which pick and shoot their own targets. That weight makes it top-heavy: -20% to Swim, Prowl, Acrobatics and Gymnastics, with -1 to initiative, Perception Rolls, dodge and roll with impact; the collar also narrows peripheral vision to about 90 degrees. Weapon Arms ERTRCS Targeting System: the Enemy Reflex Targeting and Response Computer System, quietly lifted from the Juicer Killer, recognises 4,000 enemy types (Juicers, Crazies, fast D-Bees, vampires and other supernatural beings, their armor and insignia) through cameras in the helmet, each arm and the collar, out to 5,000 ft (1,524 m), and tracks up to two targets. On ready assault the arms open fire at once; on alert they hold until the pilot orders, attacks, or is attacked. It also groups people by shared uniforms, patches or tattoos. Once the collar is down to 60 of its 120 M.D.C., roll percentile (again per further 20 points): 01-40 one arm goes off-line for a melee round; 41-60 strike bonuses halved; 61-80 no initiative bonus; 81-00 the system ignores the pilot for a melee round and picks its own target. Robot P.S. 24. Cargo: none. Power: nuclear, 12 year average life; Solid Oxide sold too. Other handheld weapons (a shotgun, side arm, Neural Mace or Vibro-Blade, or a TW, Bio-Wizard or Biomancy item) can ride on belts or in a bag. Hand to hand per Ground-Based Power Armor Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.352): restrained punch 6D6 S.D.C., normal punch 1D4 M.D., power punch 2D4 (two attacks), kick 2D6, leap kick 4D6 (two attacks); a pilot with that skill also gains +1 each to dodge and to roll with impact at levels 2, 6 and 12. Sensors beyond the standard: passive nightvision (2,000 ft/610 m) and basic recording cameras (two in the helmet, two per weapon arm, a dozen on the collar) feeding the ERTRCS. Some owners have the tech weapons converted to Techno-Wizard ones at Lazlo, New Lazlo, the Colorado Baronies or the Federation of Magic; NG builds no magic itself, though its salesmen hint. Besides the priced conversions, the sword may be swapped for any TW or other magic melee weapon. The printed length gives 2 to 1.2 m for 3.6-4 ft, about 1.1 to 1.2 m.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.83-88'),
  ('ng-xp54-enforcer-guardsman', 'Enforcer Guardsman Police Power Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One.', NULL, 'Running: 90 mph (144 km) maximum, 20% of the normal fatigue rate at high speed, 10% at 50 mph (80 km) or less. Leaping: 20 ft (6.1 m) high or across unassisted; jet-assisted up to 100 ft (30.5 m) high and 200 ft (61 m) across without flight; +30% with a running start for either. VTOL leaps: jets in the soles, behind each lower leg and on the back throw it 200 ft (61 m) up, straight or at an angle, onto vehicles, rooftops, ledges and windows up to 18 stories; it cannot ricochet between buildings as the Cougar and Lynx do, and once launched it is hard to stop or turn. No power jumping travel.', 'None. At the top of a leap it can hold a hover for 1D4 melee rounds before wobbling back down; the thrusters cushion its landings.', 'Not built for water; swims 20 mph (32 km/17.3 knots) or walks the bottom at 10 mph (16 km/8.6 knots), 20% of the normal fatigue rate. Maximum depth 500 ft (152 m).', 'Man-sized: height 6-8 ft (1.8-2.4 m); width 2-3 ft (0.6 to 0.9 m), 5 ft (1.5 m) with the light wings spread; length 3 ft (0.9 m)', '320 lbs (144 kg)', 190, 1, NULL, 600000, '1.2 million credits nuclear, 850,000 Solid Oxide, 600,000 electric battery; the lowest is stored. Optional extras: the Advanced Helmet Camera at 15,000 credits (gear row ng-xp54-advanced-helmet-camera) and the Robot Floater Camera drone at 35,000, a machine with its own stats and no row here.', 'Model Type: NG-XP54. Nicknames: SWAT Power Armor and Lawman Armor. Class: Tactical Law Enforcement Power Armor. Northern Gun''s answer to towns and agencies wanting a suit built for policing: one that can work a crime scene and still stand up to fast D-Bees, Juicers, Crazies, cyborgs, Cyber-Snatchers, Headhunters, vampires and well-armed criminals. It is meant less for beat cops than for SWAT, gang squads, rapid-response teams, detectives, and the lone sheriff with a few deputies who also runs the town militia. It carries siren and flashing lights, loudspeaker and voice modulator, spotlight, cameras, good armor, a hover-leap system, and light weapons, usually backed by the officer''s own rifle, shotgun or side arm; every unit comes with a strapped leg holster, typically carrying an energy pistol. Cat-like landings: drops up to 300 ft (91.4 m) are safe (a third of that once the back thruster is destroyed); from 300 to 600 ft (183 m) roll 1D20, and on 1-10 the suit takes 4D6 M.D. and the pilot loses 1D4 melee actions; higher drops do 2D6x10 M.D. to the suit, 1D4x10 S.D.C./Hit Points to the pilot and stun him 1D4 melee rounds. Robot P.S. 24. Cargo: none, though extra belts, pouches, holsters and a hand-carried satchel are common. Power: nuclear, 12 year average life; Solid Oxide and electric battery versions are sold. Hand to hand per Ground-Based Power Armor Training (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.352): restrained punch 6D6 S.D.C., normal punch 1D4 M.D., power punch 2D4 (two attacks), kick 2D6, leap kick 4D6 (two attacks). Features beyond the standard: Criminal I.D. Recognition System (optional, new and experimental, 89% success): facial and mark recognition through the suit, gun and Floater cameras, holding 250,000 known criminals, fugitives, Black Marketeers, terrorists and bounties plus tattoos, scars and gang colors, and anyone else whose picture is loaded. Helmet audio amplification (as the cyborg Amplified Hearing), two simple helmet cameras (96 hours of video, 8,000 stills), a language translator, multi-optics (passive nightvision and infrared 1,600 ft/488 m, ultraviolet 400 ft/122 m, telescopic 2 miles/3.2 km, x12 macro, and a camera of 100 hours and 4,000 stills), a 5 M.D.C. helmet searchlight (200 ft/61 m), a two-way radio (10 miles/16 km in town, half underground or in mountains, 20 miles/32 km in the open), and a loudspeaker with 20-voice modulator. LED Folding Light Wings (2) light a 40 ft (12.2 m) circle like day with 20 ft (6.1 m) of fading light beyond, dim or switch to ultraviolet to show blood and fluids wiped away, and move like robot arms. Police lights and siren fold out behind the hover intakes, flashing blue, red and white, with the siren aimed up and away from the pilot. Two Robot Medical Kits on the left forearm (two RAU, three RMK, two RSU and suture tape). A Universal Energy Link in each forearm powers a handheld weapon of up to 1D6x10 M.D. per blast; a breaker shuts down anything stronger. Optional Robot Floater Camera: a lunchbox-sized hovering spy drone that relays live video to up to six Guardsmen and feeds one suit''s recognition system; the M.D.C. list gives it 16, its own stat block 18.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.89-92'),
  ('ng-xf103-firefighter', 'Firefighter Power Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One.', NULL, 'Running: 80 mph (128 km) maximum, 10% of the normal fatigue rate. Leaping: 25 ft (7.6 m) high or across unassisted; jet-boosted up to 100 ft (30.5 m) high and 200 ft (61 m) across. Not flight.', 'None. A boosted leap can end in a hover of one melee round (15 seconds) before it wobbles back to the ground.', 'Not built for water; swims 20 mph (32 km/17.3 knots) or walks the bottom at 10 mph (16 km/8.6 knots), 20% of the normal fatigue rate. Maximum depth 500 ft (152 m).', 'Height 7-7.5 ft (2.1-2.3 m), 8.5 ft (2.6 m) to the top of the big tank; width 3.4 ft (1 m); length 4 ft 6 in (1.4 m)', '480 lbs (216 kg) without water tanks; printed as 525 lbs (236.2 kg) with 75 gallons (284 liters) aboard', 240, 1, NULL, 550000, '900,000 credits nuclear, 750,000 Solid Oxide, 550,000 electric; the lowest is stored. Every unit includes two loads of fire-fighting chemicals and the water cannon, and is sold with a spare pair of tanks, hose and cannon. Good availability at most NG outlets, excellent around Michigan and MercTown.', 'Model Type: NG-XF103. Class: Armored Hazard and Fire Suit. A sealed environmental suit for firefighting and search and rescue, with every standard power armor feature plus tolerance for high heat, open flame and dense smoke. A ground unit with no flight, armored well enough to shrug off falling debris and blasts, and a trusted first-response suit for close to twenty years. In the last five or six years vampire hunters of Mexico and the American Southwest have turned it, and its water cannon, against the undead. Cat-like landings: its leg thrusters make drops up to 200 ft (61 m) safe; from 200 to 400 ft (122 m) roll 1D20, and on 1-10 the suit takes 4D6 M.D. and the pilot loses 1D4 melee actions; higher drops do 2D6x10 M.D. to the suit, 1D4x10 S.D.C./Hit Points to the pilot and stun him 1D4 melee rounds. Robotic P.S. 30. Cargo: a small compartment for supplies and personal weapons; a handgun can ride in a belt, arm or chest holster. Power: nuclear, 15 year average life; Solid Oxide and electric models are sold. Hand to hand per Basic or Elite Robot Combat (Rifts Ultimate Edition p.351-352), leap kicks doing double: restrained punch 1D4 M.D., normal punch 1D6, power punch 2D6 (two attacks), kick 2D4, leap kick 4D8 (two attacks). Features beyond the standard: a thermal imager (1,000 ft/305 m) that sees through dark and smoke and finds hidden heat sources, though vampires show no heat; passive nightvision, which washes out near bright fire; rows of small colored running lights on the limbs and tanks so crews can spot each other in smoke, switchable off; heat protection to 900 C (1,652 F); 18 hours of independent oxygen; an advanced first aid kit with two each of the RAU, RMK and RSU robot medical systems on the left hip and a fireproof box of two 10-minute oxygen masks for smoke victims on the right; and a utility belt with a mini tool kit, eight mini-flares and two small green smoke grenades. The M.D.C. list prints the mini-laser as 15 each though the suit has one.', 'Rifts World Book 34: Northern Gun Two p.92-94');

